Make <intrin.h> (and through it <emmintrin.h>/<xmmintrin.h>) visible in every Lua TU, via luaconf.h.

Justification (PLAYER bytes): with VC9 /arch:SSE and no __m128 type visible, the compiler passes
the first argument of static functions in ebx (custom static convention). PLAYER does not: newlstr
0x0098cd30, luaS_newlstr 0x0098cdd0, fixjump 0x009a6740, patchlistaux 0x009a6910 and ~90 more Lua
functions only match with the intrinsics header visible (tools/lib/lua_match.py, pristine source:
360 -> 455 identical). Where it came from in 2013: the real luaconf.h includes rbx/Debug.h (for
RBXASSERT; PLAYER asserts at luaconf.h:852), which includes Base/include/RbxPlatform.h, which on
WIN32 includes <windows.h> and <intrin.h>; VC9's intrin.h includes emmintrin.h, xmmintrin.h and
mmintrin.h. <intrin.h> here and <xmmintrin.h> alone give the same bytes (both measured: 514/514).

--- a/luaconf.h
+++ b/luaconf.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 
 #include <limits.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
+#include <intrin.h>  /* ROBLOX: via rbx/Debug.h -> RbxPlatform.h */
 
 
